Test-only patch: plan Section 22 boundary cases of the Phase 2 targets that no upstream test
covers (plan step S34; human decision H3, follow-up of 2026-11-24), and boundary cases of the
public request_state.rs API R09-R12 and R15 (human decision 2026-11-25, spec-cycle review
findings sR2-a-2, sR2-b-4 and sR3-a-3)

Applies to: the copy of upstream origin/main 7caec762799bece6fba38e4298b8ca7db8bac12c after
01-request-state-wire.patch (scripts/apply-patches.sh applies formal/trusted/patches/*.patch in
file-name order, patch -p1 -F 0, only to the copy in .llbc/work/; the real source is never
patched). Files: crates/rmcp/src/model.rs, crates/rmcp/src/model/request_state.rs,
crates/rmcp/src/model/task.rs, crates/rmcp/src/transport/async_rw.rs,
crates/rmcp/src/transport/auth.rs, crates/rmcp/src/transport/common/client_side_sse.rs,
crates/rmcp/src/transport/streamable_http_server/tower.rs. Generated with git diff in a scratch
git repository holding the patch-01 copy (one hunk per file, at its end). The patch body below
is the authoritative content. 03-request-state-public.patch applies after it; its hunks
(request_state.rs lines 524-537 of the patch-01 copy) lie before the request_state.rs hunk of
this patch, so they apply at their recorded lines.

Change: #[cfg(test)] code only. Every added line lies inside a #[cfg(test)] module: at the end
of the existing test module of model.rs, model/request_state.rs (mod tests, after patch 01's
tests), model/task.rs, async_rw.rs (mod test), auth.rs and client_side_sse.rs, and in a new
#[cfg(test)] mod phase2_boundary_tests at the end of tower.rs (its added lines are one blank
separator line, the #[cfg(test)] and mod lines, and the module body, comments included).
No non-test line, no dependency, no Cargo.toml change; no existing line is removed or changed.

S34 tests (34, all files but request_state.rs): named s34_<id>_<case>; each cites its plan
Section 22 row and the Lean theorem it mirrors. Their expected values are taken from the
signed-off Lean statements and the Defs they use (Defs.parseI64, Defs.Tower.defaultPort,
Defs.Methods lists, Defs.Sse model and checks, Defs.Net definitions and checks), not from
running the code. They call the targets directly (M06/M07 pub(crate), T01-T08 and A01-A03
private: reachable only from in-module tests), so they run in the translated feature
configuration plus macros, without transport-streamable-http-client-reqwest. A test of a
feature-gated item carries the item's cfg: the M06 test
#[cfg(any(feature = "client", feature = "server"))] and the four M07 tests
#[cfg(feature = "client")], as numeric_string_value and matches_response_id (model.rs lines
321 and 329 at 7caec76); every other test calls an ungated item or lies in a module gated
already (transport/: client or server; async_rw, auth, client_side_sse, tower: their features).
So the crate's tests compile with any feature set, e.g. request-state alone (the Phase 1
evidence command). The limiter tests build every start state field by field, never through
SseEventSizeLimiter::new, which no signed-off statement covers.

R09-R12, R15 tests (12, request_state.rs, in a new mod public_api_boundaries inside mod tests,
gated by request_state.rs's own feature as the existing tests are): named after the behaviour
they pin. Their expected values are computed from the upstream source at 7caec76 (before patch
03), not from the Lean model: seal_at's expiry (line 542: now_ms.saturating_add of the TTL in
whole milliseconds clamped to i64::MAX; 0 without a TTL), the expiry check of open (line 728:
expiry != 0 && now_ms > expiry), new_with_keyring (lines 329-374), validate_key_length and
validate_config_kid (lines 755-777), with_rs1_signing and with_rs1_fallback (lines 383-442) and
the Debug impl (lines 253-276). They cover: seal_at (private; the helper of seal and seal_with,
R09/R10) with a sub-millisecond TTL, a TTL with nanoseconds, the clamp of Duration::MAX and of
i64::MAX + 1 ms and of exactly 2^64 ms, saturation near i64::MAX, negative and i64::MIN clocks,
and an expiry that lands on 0 (the token never expires and equals the token sealed without a
TTL), each checked by decoding the token's 8-byte expiry independently and by opening at the
expiry and one millisecond after it (open_at, private), also for a keyring codec that seals rs1
after with_rs1_signing; the exact InvalidKeyring messages and KeyTooShort fields of
new_with_keyring (R15) and its fault order (per entry: key id, key length, duplicate; then empty
keyring, active id validity, active id presence); the exact messages of with_rs1_signing and
with_rs1_fallback (R11, R12) on a single-key codec and for a missing kid; and their fallback
list (appended in call order, with_rs1_signing registers its own id, no duplicates, last signing
id wins) through the Debug output. open_json and open_json_with (R13, R14) get no new test. They
pass on the copy with patches 01 and 02 and with 01, 02 and 03 (patch 03 is behaviour-preserving
and changes only the bodies of seal_at and open_json_with).

Why (plan Section 19, "Tests (human decision H3)"; Section 21, H3; human decision
2026-11-25): new Rust tests of these functions must live in SDK *.rs files, which stay
byte-identical to upstream. The S34 upstream-test map (formal/trusted/evidence/README.md) found
96 uncovered and 8 partial plan Section 22 cases; this patch covers them. The spec-cycle review
of R09-R15 (findings sR2-a-2, sR2-b-4, sR3-a-3) found the expiry edges of seal_at, its rs1
keyring round trip, and the exact messages and fault order of the keyring constructors pinned by
no Rust test (the upstream test
constructor_invariants_are_enforced matches InvalidKeyring(_) and KeyTooShort { .. } only).
A test-only patch is a process exception (VERIFICATION.md Section 4 defines translation patches
as behaviour-preserving edits that make an item translate); plan Section 21 (H3) asks for it to
be recorded in formal/docs/STATUS.md, "Documents", as a further deviation from VERIFICATION.md.

Effect on the translation: none. Charon does not compile #[cfg(test)] items, and every hunk is
at the end of its file, so no translated item moves (the Source: lines of
formal/translation/ are unchanged); checked by translating the copy with patches 01-03 and
comparing it byte for byte with formal/translation/ (formal/trusted/evidence/README.md).

Evidence in CI: patched-tests.yml runs cargo test --locked --lib on the copy with all patches
(translated features plus macros, overflow checks and debug assertions on), which runs these
tests. Delete this patch if the tests land in the SDK source.
